{{#extend "layout" showSource=true}}

  {{#content "main"}}
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Example 6 &middot; sitemap</p>
    <h1>{{model.heading}}</h1>
    <p>{{model.lede}}</p>
  </section>

  <div class="grid">
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Home</h2>
      <p class="meta">Listed, with no date</p>
      <p>The default: a page with no date of its own is listed without a <code>&lt;lastmod&gt;</code>.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>About</h2>
      <p class="meta">Listed, with no date</p>
      <p><a href="about/index.html">Open the about page</a></p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Stockists</h2>
      <p class="meta">Listed, last modified 2026-10-14</p>
      <p><a href="stockists/index.html">Open the stockists page</a></p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Roasting rota</h2>
      <p class="meta tone-warn">Built and served, but not listed</p>
      <p><a href="rota/index.html">Open the rota</a> — then look for it in the sitemap.</p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <div class="callout">
    <p><a href="sitemap.xml">Read the generated sitemap.xml</a></p>
  </div>
  {{/content}}

  {{#content "demo"}}
  <p>
    <code>.sitemap()</code> writes <code>sitemap.xml</code> from the pages already
    registered, so nothing is listed twice and nothing is invented. It needs
    <code>siteUrl</code> in the config to turn each page into an absolute URL; without one
    it logs an error and skips the file.
  </p>
  <p>
    The rota sets <code>ignoreSitemap</code> and drops out of the file entirely. The
    stockists page's model carries <code>updated</code>, the date the list last changed,
    and that is its <code>&lt;lastmod&gt;</code>; the pages with no date state none, because
    a date that moves on every build is one a search engine learns to ignore.
    <code>extensionLess</code> is a whole-site setting: pages build to
    <code>about/index.html</code>, so the sitemap advertises tidy folder URLs.
  </p>
  {{/content}}

{{/extend}}
